Regress: Fill in initial Drawz with Draw for display, normal, depth, identity. Add change of Drawz args upon UnifMsk and Buffer write. Couple Focal* registers with projection matrix. Finish Demo and use it in planer.lua. Write random triangles. Do following spoofs with appropriate delays. Spoof change to inactive/polytope/rotate mode. Spoof click on one of the triangles to get pierce point and change to active/polytope/rotate mode. Spoof move cursor and roller several times to transform. Spoof timer event to send.  Send as if from other. Send loopback. Send more from other. Do same for other modes.

Release: Use actual user actions to interact with actual file. Finish spaceHs to keep track of boundaries and regions. Add maintenate of cospace boundaries, with all internal regions. Removing a cospace boundary removes three space boundaries, which in turn removes other cospace boundaries.

Doodle: Add click mode that adds plane perpendicular to facet at pierce point, with roller mode that rotates the plane around the normal, and decorates divided facets on one side of the new plane differently from on the other. Add register to identify Express Memory for getting new decorations from divided decorations. Bind number keys to choose which Express used to decorate each side of a divided facet.

Decoration: Add struct and Memory to contain info for custom shaders. Switch on uniform field to decide whether to apply texture or whatever. Fragment shader little language follows graph edges depending on inputs from vertex shader for filling with a constant, copying color or depth or identifier from vertex shader, copying from image buffer, applying texture sampler, calculating from normal, highlighting from adjacent identifiers. Graph edges are constants/inputs in which hypersquare region of constants/inputs, or on which hyperline sids of constants/inputs.

Suite: In plane.lua, share, file, space, plane, side to manipulate polytopes. In space.lua, share, file, space, plane, to display tetrahedron overlaps as they are found and optimized. In line.lua, share, file, space, plane, line, side, to decorate polytopes with sound. In point.lua, share, file, space, plane, line, side, frame, to decorate facets with little language for textures, sound, frames, text, graffiti, doodles, permissions, wormholes, transparency. Share connects processes by pipe. Side displays and edits fields in file. Frame displays and edits video and interfaces to hdmi over usbc.

Compositor: Use wlroots to add previews of irregularly bounded windows to facets of a polytope created with plane from the suite. Add click mode to make the clicked window facet part of the tiled background. Add roller mode to fade the foreground polytope in and out. Add way to switch keyboard mouse between foreground polytope and background window tiles.

Name: Call the application pball, for polytope ballet. Higher dimensional spaces are simpler than lower. They teach real analysis with blobs of various sort, like open covering compact and so on, because blobs are easier to understand than numbers. Topology is cool and all, but there is not as much to it as there is to real or even complex numbers. The beauty of two dimensional complex analysis is that complex numbers are simpler than real numbers. What is harder to understand than one dimensional real numbers? The relation or interface of math to reality is zero dimensional and harder to understand than either in isolation. But that’s just metaphysics, so who cares? I just think it’s neat.
